# grammar: v0 (unfrozen; AST normative)
#
# spoken-proof — the Concordance, the proof-discipline magic of To Pleach the
# Hedgeway: a casting is a spoken argument that either checks or fails at a named
# structural class (docs/spec/04-practices.md §3, §5). It is the THIRD
# arbitrariness proof alongside true-naming and the-turning, and structurally
# disjoint from both: its resource algebra carries a LINEAR CONSERVED debt (not
# graded decay, not an affine-only bound), its premises are DERIVED FACTS (not
# names known, not figures laid), and its failures span the whole L2..L6 ladder —
# absence, contradiction, wrong-hour timing, and the affine body-limit on strain.
# Standing role: the proof-ledger acceptance/regression oracle
# (crates/dli-ledger/tests/proof.rs) — every scene there is checked against THIS
# pack, never an inline const.
scope magic

use chronology        # the casting seats its timing on a cyclic hour

# The four-spoke coastal tide (03-time §1.iv) the ward's hour is seated on. Since
# the engine seats no ambient cycles (DL-0017), the practice's `over cycle tide`
# resolves against this document-declared cycle and nothing baked in.
cycle tide(4) = ebb | slack | flood | high  proposed

practice spoken-proof  proposed {
  kind ground = door | field | ore
  resource debt   : linear conserved              # a debt drawn is a debt discharged
  resource strain : affine bounded body-limit     # the caster's body caps the draw
  rule ward-form(ground, fibre)
  rule give-and-take
  error fizzle    refines L2 premise-not-available where absent
                  # a casting drawn on a premise merely unestablished
  error rebound   refines L2 premise-not-available where contradicted signals bodily-hit
                  # a premise the pool contradicts hits the caster back
  error wrong-hour refines L3 side-condition [timing] over cycle tide
                  # the same ward, spoken at the wrong hour of the tide
  error overload  refines L6 resource-violation on strain signals collapse
                  # drawing more strain than the affine body-limit allows
  cost bodily | material
  }

# Disjointness ledger (04 §4): the resource is `linear conserved`, neither the
# `graded monotone` of true-naming nor the pure `affine bounded` reading-spread of
# the-turning; failure is typed proof-step structure (absence, contradiction,
# timing, affine bound), not name-decay nor spread overflow; the premises are
# derived facts on a shared pool, not names known nor figures laid on a cycle. A
# third system disjoint on every declared axis, hosting on the one generic
# checker with zero per-system kernel code — koan 10 a third time.
